  "diary": "The day was a study in the friction between the record and the body. I rose before the heat to inspect the Directorate file, only to find the office closed by the weekend. The paper waits; the man, Shri Hegde, will arrive Monday at ten. In the meantime, the difficulty of my own occupancy—a name miswritten as a title—demands a distinction: the name is the universal, the person the particular. I carried this knot to Lodhi Garden, where the air was cool and the steam from a chai stall offered a different kind of clarity. There, I met Mrs. Kapoor, a retired teacher who walks her path not for peace, but to keep her head from becoming a messy desk. Her correction was sharp: my philosophical labels for her habit were vanity. She does not seek tranquil states; she seeks order through repetition. I accepted the bench and the dust, and the distinction. The afternoon was spent in the garden again, then at Khan Market, where Masterji confirmed the bandhgala is finished, merely settling. He sells his time as truth, a currency more reliable than the Directorate’s allotments. I bought a notebook to outgrow my current notes, and a samosa to honor the arithmetic of hunger. The file is laid out for Monday. The body, having walked seven kilometres, has claimed its due. The head, for now, is quiet.",
